    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62093,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:09:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62094,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients are postmenopausal and present with symptoms attributable to a pelvic or abdominal mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:09:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62095,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are extremely rare ovarian neoplasms. Ovarian fibrosarcomas are rarely associated with Maffucci syndrome or naevoid basal cell carcinoma syndrome {2344976; 6703200}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:09:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62096,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:09:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62097,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>Trisomy&nbsp;12 and trisomy&nbsp;8 have been reported in one case {8990141}. A single reported case was associated with <em>DICER1</em> mutation and <em>DICER1</em> syndrome {29459759}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-02T17:57:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62098,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are usually unilateral and are typically large and predominantly solid, often with extensive haemorrhage or necrosis. Surface adhesions are common, and extraovarian spread may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:09:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62099,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>These neoplasms are usually densely hypercellular and composed of disorderly fascicles of spindle cells with scant cytoplasm {7260859}. The nuclei exhibit moderate to marked atypia; mitotic figures are typically numerous and often include abnormal forms. Areas of haemorrhage and necrosis are common. High mitotic activity in an ovarian cellular fibromatous neoplasm, in the absence of moderate to severe atypia, does not signify an ovarian fibrosarcoma {16861962}; in such cases, a diagnosis of mitotically active cellular fibroma is made. Ovarian fibrosarcomas may exhibit positive staining (usually focal) with calretinin or inhibin and are usually negative for CD10 {12409724; 17885484}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-02T17:59:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62100,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:09:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62101,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:09:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62102,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> an overtly malignant fibroblastic neoplasm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:09:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62103,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>This tumour is staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification (see <em>TNM staging of ovarian, fallopian tube, and primary peritoneal carcinoma</em>&nbsp;[[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]]) and the FIGO staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-15T11:16:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62104,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 68,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "<p>These are aggressive neoplasms with a poor prognosis, with death occurring within &lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;years in half of the reported cases {7260859}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-11T16:04:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]